module

public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Blowup.ReesSheafData
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Blowup.Existence
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.AffineBlowup.ModelComparison
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Blowup.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Blowup.Defs

/-!
# The affine charts of a blowup are spectra of affine blowup algebras

Let `R` be a commutative ring and `I ⊆ R` an ideal. For `a ∈ I` write `a⁽¹⁾` for `a` seen as an
element of degree one of the Rees algebra `R[It] = ⨁_{n ≥ 0} Iⁿ`, whose grading is
`Stacks.Blowup.reesGrading`. This file identifies the standard affine chart `D₊(a⁽¹⁾)` of
`Proj (R[It])` with the spectrum of the affine blowup algebra `R[I/a]`, and deduces that the
preimage of an affine open `U` under a blowup morphism is covered by the spectra of the affine
blowup algebras `Γ(S, U)[ℐ(U)/a]`.

Together with `Stacks.Blowup.isPullback_blowUpChart`, which identifies `b⁻¹(U)` with
`Proj (Γ(S, U)[ℐ(U)t])`, this is Stacks tag 0804: the first assertion is the identification with
`Proj`, the second is the affine covering supplied here.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Blowup.reesToAway` is the evaluation `R[It] → R_a`, `monomial n r ↦ r / aⁿ`.
* `Stacks.Blowup.reesAwayMk` is the fraction `r / aⁿ`, `r ∈ Iⁿ`, in the chart.
* `Stacks.Blowup.reesAwayToAway` is the chart map `(R[It])_{(a⁽¹⁾)} → R_a`.
* `Stacks.Blowup.specAffineBlowupι` is the open immersion `Spec R[I/a] ⟶ Proj (R[It])`.
* `Stacks.Blowup.blowUpAffineChart` is the affine chart `Spec Γ(S, U)[ℐ(U)/a] ⟶ X'` of a blowup.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Blowup.reesAwayEquivAffineBlowup`: the degree-zero part of the localization of the Rees
  algebra at `a⁽¹⁾` is the affine blowup algebra `R[I/a]`. This is the chart half of Stacks tag
  0804.
* `Stacks.Blowup.iSup_opensRange_specAffineBlowupι`: the charts `Spec R[I/a]`, for `a ∈ I`, cover
  `Proj (R[It])`.
* `Stacks.Blowup.iSup_opensRange_blowUpAffineChart`: the preimage of an affine open `U` under the
  blowup morphism is covered by the images of the `Spec Γ(S, U)[ℐ(U)/a]`. This is the second
  assertion of Stacks tag 0804.
* `Stacks.Blowup.reesAwayEquivAffineBlowup_fromZeroRingHom`: the chart identification is
  compatible with the structure maps over the base.
* `Stacks.Blowup.algebraMap_affineBlowup_mem_nonZeroDivisors` and
  `Stacks.Blowup.affineBlowup_idealMap_eq_span`: on the chart `Spec R[I/a]` the inverse image of
  the centre of the blowup is generated by the image of `a`, which is a nonzerodivisor. These are
  the two statements of Stacks tag 07Z3 that the proof of Stacks tag 02OS consumes, for the
  `affineBlowup` realization of `R[I/a]`.

## Implementation notes

The target of the chart identification is `affineBlowup I a`, the affine blowup algebra as the
`R`-subalgebra of `Localization.Away a` generated by the fractions `x / a` with `x ∈ I`
(`StacksFrontier/RingTheory/Blowup/Basic.lean`); that it is the subalgebra carrying the
`@[stacks 052Q]` attribute is `affineBlowup_eq_affineBlowupAlgebra` in
`StacksFrontier/RingTheory/AffineBlowup/ModelComparison.lean`, which identifies all five
realizations of `R[I/a]` in this development.

The identification is recorded as a `RingEquiv`, not an `AlgEquiv`: an `R`-algebra structure on
`HomogeneousLocalization.Away (reesGrading I) a⁽¹⁾` is not found by instance search, because the
base ring has to be routed through `Stacks.Blowup.reesGradingZeroEquiv`. The `R`-algebra
structure that does exist is the one installed in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Blowup/AwayBaseChange.lean`; nothing here needs it.

The map out of the chart is built from the evaluation `reesToAway`, which sends the degree-one
element `a⁽¹⁾` to `1`; the universal property of `Localization.Away` then factors it through the
localization at `a⁽¹⁾`, and the homogeneous localization sits inside that localization by
`HomogeneousLocalization.val_injective`. Both halves of bijectivity are read off the single
presentation `reesAwayMk`: surjectivity from `affineBlowup_mem_iff` and injectivity from
`reesAwayMk_eq_iff`, whose right-hand side is literally the one of `affineBlowup_repr_eq_iff`.

For the covering statement, `Proj.iSup_basicOpen_eq_top'` asks for generation in degree one over
the degree-zero part `reesGrading I 0`, while `adjoin_reesGrading_one_eq_top` provides it over
`R`. There is no `IsScalarTower R (reesGrading I 0) (reesAlgebra I)` instance, so the transfer is
done by `Algebra.adjoin_induction` in `adjoin_reesGradingZero_reesGrading_one_eq_top` rather than
through `Subalgebra.restrictScalars`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 052Q](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/052Q)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0804](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0804)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory HomogeneousLocalization Polynomial

universe u

namespace Stacks.Blowup

variable {R : Type u} [CommRing R] (I : Ideal R) (a : R)

/-! ### The chart ring -/

/-- The evaluation `R[It] → R_a` of the Rees algebra at `1/a`: it sends the degree-`n` monomial
`monomial n r` to the fraction `r / aⁿ`. -/
def reesToAway : reesAlgebra I →ₐ[R] Localization.Away a :=
  (Polynomial.aeval (IsLocalization.Away.invSelf a)).comp (reesAlgebra I).val

/-- The fraction `r / aⁿ` of `R_a` written through `1/a`. -/
theorem mk_eq_algebraMap_mul_invSelf_pow (n : ℕ) (r : R) :
    (Localization.mk r ⟨a ^ n, n, rfl⟩ : Localization.Away a)
      = algebraMap R (Localization.Away a) r * IsLocalization.Away.invSelf a ^ n := by
  rw [IsLocalization.Away.invSelf, ← Localization.mk_eq_mk', ← Localization.mk_one_eq_algebraMap,
    Localization.mk_pow, Localization.mk_mul]
  congr 1
  · ring
  · exact Subtype.ext (by simp)

/-- The evaluation sends the degree-`n` part of the Rees algebra to the fractions `r / aⁿ`. -/
theorem reesToAway_reesMonomial (n : ℕ) (r : (I ^ n : Ideal R)) :
    reesToAway I a (reesMonomial I n r)
      = (Localization.mk (r : R) ⟨a ^ n, n, rfl⟩ : Localization.Away a) := by
  rw [mk_eq_algebraMap_mul_invSelf_pow]
  simp [reesToAway, Polynomial.aeval_monomial]

/-- The evaluation sends `a⁽¹⁾` to `1`. -/
theorem reesToAway_reesDegOne (ha : a ∈ I) : reesToAway I a (reesDegOne I ha) = 1 := by
  simp [reesToAway, coe_reesDegOne, Polynomial.aeval_monomial, IsLocalization.Away.mul_invSelf]

/-- The image of `a⁽¹⁾` under the evaluation is a unit, so the evaluation factors through the
localization of the Rees algebra at `a⁽¹⁾`. -/
theorem isUnit_reesToAway_reesDegOne (ha : a ∈ I) :
    IsUnit ((reesToAway I a).toRingHom (reesDegOne I ha)) := by
  rw [AlgHom.toRingHom_eq_coe, RingHom.coe_coe, reesToAway_reesDegOne]
  exact isUnit_one

/-- The chart map `(R[It])_{(a⁽¹⁾)} → R_a`: the degree-zero part of the localization of the Rees
algebra at `a⁽¹⁾` sits inside that localization, which maps to `R_a` by the evaluation at `1/a`.
It is injective with image the affine blowup algebra `R[I/a]`; see
`Stacks.Blowup.reesAwayEquivAffineBlowup`. -/
def reesAwayToAway (ha : a ∈ I) :
    Away (reesGrading I) (reesDegOne I ha) →+* Localization.Away a :=
  (IsLocalization.Away.lift (S := Localization.Away (reesDegOne I ha))
      (reesDegOne I ha) (isUnit_reesToAway_reesDegOne I a ha)).comp
    (algebraMap (Away (reesGrading I) (reesDegOne I ha))
      (Localization (Submonoid.powers (reesDegOne I ha))))

/-- The chart map on a fraction with homogeneous numerator: since `a⁽¹⁾` is sent to `1`, the
denominator disappears. -/
theorem reesAwayToAway_mk (ha : a ∈ I) (n : ℕ) (x : reesAlgebra I)
    (hx : x ∈ reesGrading I (n • 1)) :
    reesAwayToAway I a ha (Away.mk (reesGrading I) (reesDegOne_mem_reesGrading I ha) n x hx)
      = reesToAway I a x := by
  rw [reesAwayToAway, RingHom.comp_apply, HomogeneousLocalization.algebraMap_apply,
    Away.val_mk, Localization.mk_eq_mk', IsLocalization.Away.lift,
    IsLocalization.lift_mk'_spec]
  simp [map_pow, reesToAway_reesDegOne]

/-- The fraction `r / aⁿ`, for `r ∈ Iⁿ`, as an element of the chart `(R[It])_{(a⁽¹⁾)}`. -/
def reesAwayMk (ha : a ∈ I) (n : ℕ) (r : (I ^ n : Ideal R)) :
    Away (reesGrading I) (reesDegOne I ha) :=
  Away.mk (reesGrading I) (reesDegOne_mem_reesGrading I ha) n (reesMonomial I n r)
    (by rw [smul_eq_mul, mul_one]; exact (reesMonomial I n r).2)

/-- The chart map sends `r / aⁿ` to `r / aⁿ`. -/
theorem reesAwayToAway_reesAwayMk (ha : a ∈ I) (n : ℕ) (r : (I ^ n : Ideal R)) :
    reesAwayToAway I a ha (reesAwayMk I a ha n r)
      = (Localization.mk (r : R) ⟨a ^ n, n, rfl⟩ : Localization.Away a) := by
  rw [reesAwayMk, reesAwayToAway_mk, reesToAway_reesMonomial]

/-- Every element of the chart `(R[It])_{(a⁽¹⁾)}` is a fraction `r / aⁿ` with `r ∈ Iⁿ`. -/
theorem reesAwayMk_surjective (ha : a ∈ I) (z : Away (reesGrading I) (reesDegOne I ha)) :
    ∃ (n : ℕ) (r : (I ^ n : Ideal R)), reesAwayMk I a ha n r = z := by
  obtain ⟨n, x, hx, rfl⟩ := Away.mk_surjective (reesGrading I) (reesDegOne_mem_reesGrading I ha) z
  have hx' : x ∈ reesGrading I n := by simpa using hx
  refine ⟨n, ⟨(x : R[X]).coeff n, x.2 n⟩, ?_⟩
  apply HomogeneousLocalization.val_injective
  rw [reesAwayMk, Away.val_mk, Away.val_mk]
  congr 1
  exact Subtype.ext (coe_eq_monomial I hx').symm

/-- Multiplying a homogeneous element by a power of `a⁽¹⁾` multiplies its coefficient by the
corresponding power of `a` and shifts its degree. -/
theorem coe_reesDegOne_pow_mul (ha : a ∈ I) (k j : ℕ) (x : reesAlgebra I) (p : R)
    (hp : (x : R[X]) = monomial j p) :
    ((reesDegOne I ha ^ k * x : reesAlgebra I) : R[X]) = monomial (k + j) (a ^ k * p) := by
  rw [Subalgebra.coe_mul, Subalgebra.coe_pow, coe_reesDegOne, hp, Polynomial.monomial_pow,
    Polynomial.monomial_mul_monomial, one_mul]

/-- Two fractions `r / aⁿ` and `s / aᵐ` agree in the chart `(R[It])_{(a⁽¹⁾)}` exactly when
`aᵏ (aᵐ r - aⁿ s) = 0` in `R` for some `k`, which is the equality criterion of the affine blowup
algebra recorded in `affineBlowup_repr_eq_iff`. -/
theorem reesAwayMk_eq_iff (ha : a ∈ I) {n m : ℕ} (r : (I ^ n : Ideal R)) (s : (I ^ m : Ideal R)) :
    reesAwayMk I a ha n r = reesAwayMk I a ha m s ↔
      ∃ k : ℕ, a ^ k * (a ^ m * r - a ^ n * s) = 0 := by
  have h : ∀ (k i j : ℕ) (t : (I ^ j : Ideal R)),
      ((reesDegOne I ha ^ k * (reesDegOne I ha ^ i * reesMonomial I j t) : reesAlgebra I) : R[X])
        = monomial (k + (i + j)) (a ^ k * (a ^ i * t)) := fun k i j t =>
    coe_reesDegOne_pow_mul I a ha k (i + j) _ _
      (coe_reesDegOne_pow_mul I a ha i j _ _ (coe_reesMonomial I t))
  have key : ∀ k : ℕ, reesDegOne I ha ^ k * (reesDegOne I ha ^ m * reesMonomial I n r)
        = reesDegOne I ha ^ k * (reesDegOne I ha ^ n * reesMonomial I m s) ↔
      a ^ k * (a ^ m * r - a ^ n * s) = 0 := fun k => by
    rw [Subtype.ext_iff, h, h, add_comm n m, (Polynomial.monomial_injective _).eq_iff, mul_sub,
      sub_eq_zero]
  rw [HomogeneousLocalization.ext_iff_val, reesAwayMk, reesAwayMk, Away.val_mk, Away.val_mk,
    Localization.mk_eq_mk_iff, Localization.r_iff_exists]
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨⟨_, k, rfl⟩, hc⟩
    exact ⟨k, (key k).mp hc⟩
  · rintro ⟨k, hk⟩
    exact ⟨⟨_, k, rfl⟩, (key k).mpr hk⟩

/-- The chart map lands in the affine blowup algebra. -/
theorem reesAwayToAway_mem_affineBlowup (ha : a ∈ I)
    (z : Away (reesGrading I) (reesDegOne I ha)) :
    reesAwayToAway I a ha z ∈ affineBlowup I a := by
  obtain ⟨n, r, rfl⟩ := reesAwayMk_surjective I a ha z
  rw [reesAwayToAway_reesAwayMk]
  exact mk_mem_affineBlowup_of_mem_pow I a r.2

/-- The chart map `reesAwayToAway I a ha` is injective. -/
theorem reesAwayToAway_injective (ha : a ∈ I) : Function.Injective (reesAwayToAway I a ha) := by
  intro z w h
  obtain ⟨n, r, rfl⟩ := reesAwayMk_surjective I a ha z
  obtain ⟨m, s, rfl⟩ := reesAwayMk_surjective I a ha w
  rw [reesAwayToAway_reesAwayMk, reesAwayToAway_reesAwayMk, affineBlowup_repr_eq_iff] at h
  exact (reesAwayMk_eq_iff I a ha r s).mpr h

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0804.** For `a ∈ I` the standard affine chart of `Proj` of the Rees
algebra at the degree-one element `a⁽¹⁾` is the affine blowup algebra `R[I/a]`: the degree-zero
part of the localization of `R[It]` at `a⁽¹⁾` is `R[I/a]`.

This is the chart computation behind the second assertion of tag 0804; the covering statement
itself is `Stacks.Blowup.iSup_opensRange_blowUpAffineChart`. -/
@[stacks 0804 "the chart D₊(a⁽¹⁾) is Spec of the affine blowup algebra"]
def reesAwayEquivAffineBlowup (ha : a ∈ I) :
    Away (reesGrading I) (reesDegOne I ha) ≃+* affineBlowup I a :=
  RingEquiv.ofBijective ((reesAwayToAway I a ha).codRestrict (affineBlowup I a)
      (reesAwayToAway_mem_affineBlowup I a ha))
    ⟨RingHom.injective_codRestrict.mpr (reesAwayToAway_injective I a ha), by
      rintro ⟨z, hz⟩
      obtain ⟨n, x, hx, rfl⟩ := (affineBlowup_mem_iff I a ha z).mp hz
      exact ⟨reesAwayMk I a ha n ⟨x, hx⟩,
        Subtype.ext (reesAwayToAway_reesAwayMk I a ha n ⟨x, hx⟩)⟩⟩

/-- The chart identification, read on fractions: `r / aⁿ` goes to `r / aⁿ`. -/
theorem coe_reesAwayEquivAffineBlowup_reesAwayMk (ha : a ∈ I) (n : ℕ) (r : (I ^ n : Ideal R)) :
    ((reesAwayEquivAffineBlowup I a ha (reesAwayMk I a ha n r) : affineBlowup I a) :
        Localization.Away a)
      = (Localization.mk (r : R) ⟨a ^ n, n, rfl⟩ : Localization.Away a) :=
  reesAwayToAway_reesAwayMk I a ha n r

/-- The degree-zero identification of the Rees algebra sends `r` to the constant polynomial. -/
theorem reesGradingZeroEquiv_apply (r : R) :
    reesGradingZeroEquiv I r = algebraMap R (reesGrading I 0) r := rfl

/-- The inverse of the degree-zero identification of the Rees algebra reads off the constant
coefficient. -/
theorem reesGradingZeroEquiv_symm_apply (z : reesGrading I 0) :
    (reesGradingZeroEquiv I).symm z = ((z : reesAlgebra I) : R[X]).coeff 0 := by
  apply (reesGradingZeroEquiv I).injective
  rw [RingEquiv.apply_symm_apply, reesGradingZeroEquiv_apply]
  refine Subtype.ext (Subtype.ext ?_)
  rw [SetLike.GradeZero.coe_algebraMap]
  simpa [Polynomial.monomial_zero_left] using coe_eq_monomial I z.2

/-- The structure map of the chart over the degree-zero part of the Rees algebra is the fraction
with denominator `a⁰`. -/
theorem fromZeroRingHom_eq_reesAwayMk (ha : a ∈ I) (z : reesGrading I 0) :
    fromZeroRingHom (reesGrading I) (Submonoid.powers (reesDegOne I ha)) z
      = reesAwayMk I a ha 0 ⟨((z : reesAlgebra I) : R[X]).coeff 0, (z : reesAlgebra I).2 0⟩ := by
  apply HomogeneousLocalization.val_injective
  rw [reesAwayMk, Away.val_mk]
  show Localization.mk (z : reesAlgebra I) 1 = _
  congr 1
  refine Subtype.ext ?_
  rw [coe_reesMonomial]
  simpa [Polynomial.monomial_zero_left] using coe_eq_monomial I z.2

/-- **The chart identification is compatible with the structure maps over the base.** The
structure map of the chart `(R[It])_{(a⁽¹⁾)}` over the degree-zero part `reesGrading I 0 ≅ R` of
the Rees algebra corresponds to the structure map `R → R[I/a]` of the affine blowup algebra.

Together with `AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.awayι_toSpecZero` this is what identifies the morphism
`Spec R[I/a] ⟶ Proj (R[It]) ⟶ Spec R` with `Spec` of the structure map, which is the remaining
input of Stacks tag 02OS. -/
theorem reesAwayEquivAffineBlowup_fromZeroRingHom (ha : a ∈ I) (z : reesGrading I 0) :
    reesAwayEquivAffineBlowup I a ha
        (fromZeroRingHom (reesGrading I) (Submonoid.powers (reesDegOne I ha)) z)
      = algebraMap R (affineBlowup I a) ((reesGradingZeroEquiv I).symm z) := by
  refine Subtype.ext ?_
  rw [fromZeroRingHom_eq_reesAwayMk, coe_reesAwayEquivAffineBlowup_reesAwayMk,
    reesGradingZeroEquiv_symm_apply]
  show _ = algebraMap R (Localization.Away a) _
  rw [← Localization.mk_one_eq_algebraMap]
  congr 1
  exact Subtype.ext (by simp)

/-! ### The ideal of the exceptional divisor on a chart -/

/-- The image of `a` in `R[I/a]` is a nonzerodivisor: it is already a unit in the ambient
localization `R_a`. This is Stacks tag 07Z3 (1) for `affineBlowup`; the tagged statement
`blowup_image_a_mem_nonZeroDivisors` is the same fact for the quotient realization `Blowup I a`
of `R[I/a]`. -/
theorem algebraMap_affineBlowup_mem_nonZeroDivisors :
    algebraMap R (affineBlowup I a) a ∈ nonZeroDivisors (affineBlowup I a) := by
  rw [mem_nonZeroDivisors_iff_right]
  intro w hw
  have hcoe : (w : Localization.Away a) * algebraMap R (Localization.Away a) a = 0 := by
    simpa using congrArg (fun t : affineBlowup I a => (t : Localization.Away a)) hw
  obtain ⟨u, hu⟩ := IsLocalization.Away.algebraMap_isUnit (S := Localization.Away a) a
  apply Subtype.coe_injective
  rw [← hu] at hcoe
  simpa using (Units.mul_left_eq_zero u).mp hcoe

/-- The ideal of `R[I/a]` generated by the image of `I` is generated by the image of `a`, so the
inverse image of the centre of the blowup is principal on the chart `Spec R[I/a]`. This is Stacks
tag 07Z3 (2) for `affineBlowup`; the tagged statement `blowup_idealMap_eq_span` is the same fact
for the quotient realization `Blowup I a` of `R[I/a]`. -/
theorem affineBlowup_idealMap_eq_span (ha : a ∈ I) :
    Ideal.map (algebraMap R (affineBlowup I a)) I
      = Ideal.span {algebraMap R (affineBlowup I a) a} := by
  refine le_antisymm ?_ ?_
  · rw [Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap]
    intro y hy
    rw [Ideal.mem_comap, Ideal.mem_span_singleton]
    refine ⟨⟨Localization.mk y ⟨a, Submonoid.mem_powers a⟩,
      Algebra.subset_adjoin ⟨y, hy, rfl⟩⟩, ?_⟩
    apply Subtype.coe_injective
    show algebraMap R (Localization.Away a) y
      = algebraMap R (Localization.Away a) a * Localization.mk y ⟨a, Submonoid.mem_powers a⟩
    rw [← Localization.mk_one_eq_algebraMap, ← Localization.mk_one_eq_algebraMap,
      Localization.mk_mul, Localization.mk_eq_mk_iff, Localization.r_iff_exists]
    exact ⟨1, by simp⟩
  · rw [Ideal.span_le, Set.singleton_subset_iff, SetLike.mem_coe]
    exact Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ ha

/-! ### The charts cover `Proj` of the Rees algebra -/

/-- The degree-one elements of the Rees algebra are exactly the `a⁽¹⁾` for `a ∈ I`. -/
theorem range_reesDegOne :
    Set.range (fun r : I => reesDegOne I r.2)
      = ((reesGrading I 1 : Submodule R (reesAlgebra I)) : Set (reesAlgebra I)) := by
  ext f
  refine ⟨?_, fun hf => ?_⟩
  · rintro ⟨r, rfl⟩
    exact reesDegOne_mem_reesGrading I r.2
  · exact ⟨⟨(f : R[X]).coeff 1, by simpa using f.2 1⟩,
      Subtype.ext (coe_eq_monomial I hf).symm⟩

/-- **The standard affine opens `D₊(a⁽¹⁾)`, `a ∈ I`, cover `Proj` of the Rees algebra.** This is
the first step of the proof of the second assertion of Stacks tag 0804: the Rees algebra is
generated by its degree-one part, a copy of `I`. -/
theorem iSup_basicOpen_reesDegOne_eq_top :
    ⨆ r : I, Proj.basicOpen (reesGrading I) (reesDegOne I r.2) = ⊤ :=
  Proj.iSup_basicOpen_eq_top' _ _ (fun r => ⟨1, reesDegOne_mem_reesGrading I r.2⟩)
    (by rw [range_reesDegOne]; exact adjoin_reesGradingZero_reesGrading_one_eq_top I)

/-- The standard affine chart of `Proj` of the Rees algebra attached to `a ∈ I`, as a morphism
out of the spectrum of the affine blowup algebra `R[I/a]`. It is an open immersion with image
`D₊(a⁽¹⁾)`. -/
def specAffineBlowupι (ha : a ∈ I) :
    Spec (CommRingCat.of (affineBlowup I a)) ⟶ Proj (reesGrading I) :=
  Spec.map (reesAwayEquivAffineBlowup I a ha).toCommRingCatIso.hom ≫
    Proj.awayι (reesGrading I) (reesDegOne I ha) (reesDegOne_mem_reesGrading I ha) Nat.one_pos

/-- The chart `specAffineBlowupι I a ha` is an open immersion. -/
instance (ha : a ∈ I) : IsOpenImmersion (specAffineBlowupι I a ha) :=
  IsOpenImmersion.comp _ _

/-- The chart `Spec R[I/a]` is the standard affine open `D₊(a⁽¹⁾)` of `Proj` of the Rees
algebra. -/
theorem opensRange_specAffineBlowupι (ha : a ∈ I) :
    (specAffineBlowupι I a ha).opensRange =
      Proj.basicOpen (reesGrading I) (reesDegOne I ha) :=
  (Scheme.Hom.opensRange_comp_of_isIso _ _).trans
    (Proj.opensRange_awayι (reesGrading I) _ (reesDegOne_mem_reesGrading I ha) Nat.one_pos)

/-- **The spectra of the affine blowup algebras `R[I/a]`, `a ∈ I`, cover `Proj` of the Rees
algebra.** This is the local form of the second assertion of Stacks tag 0804. -/
theorem iSup_opensRange_specAffineBlowupι :
    ⨆ r : I, (specAffineBlowupι I (r : R) r.2).opensRange = ⊤ := by
  simpa only [opensRange_specAffineBlowupι] using iSup_basicOpen_reesDegOne_eq_top I

/-! ### The charts of the blowup of a scheme -/

variable {S : Scheme.{u}} (ℐ : S.IdealSheafData)

/-- The preimage of an affine open `U` of the base in the blowup is the image of the chart of the
blowup over `U`. -/
theorem blowUpToBase_preimage_coe (U : S.affineOpens) :
    blowUpToBase ℐ ⁻¹ᵁ (U : S.Opens) = (blowUpChart ℐ U).opensRange :=
  (reesData ℐ).toBase_preimage_coe U

/-- The affine chart of the blowup attached to an affine open `U` of the base and a section
`a ∈ ℐ(U)`: the spectrum of the affine blowup algebra `Γ(S, U)[ℐ(U)/a]`, as an open subscheme of
the blowup. -/
def blowUpAffineChart (U : S.affineOpens) {a : Γ(S, U.1)} (ha : a ∈ ℐ.ideal U) :
    Spec (CommRingCat.of (affineBlowup (ℐ.ideal U) a)) ⟶ blowUp ℐ :=
  specAffineBlowupι (ℐ.ideal U) a ha ≫ blowUpChart ℐ U

/-- The affine chart `blowUpAffineChart ℐ U ha` of the blowup is an open immersion. -/
instance (U : S.affineOpens) {a : Γ(S, U.1)} (ha : a ∈ ℐ.ideal U) :
    IsOpenImmersion (blowUpAffineChart ℐ U ha) :=
  IsOpenImmersion.comp _ _

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0804, second assertion.** Let `b : X' ⟶ S` be the blowup of a scheme
`S` in a quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals `ℐ`, and let `U` be an affine open of `S`. Then `b⁻¹(U)`
is covered by the spectra of the affine blowup algebras `Γ(S, U)[ℐ(U)/a]` for `a ∈ ℐ(U)`: the
morphisms `Stacks.Blowup.blowUpAffineChart` are open immersions whose images have supremum
`b⁻¹(U)`.

Together with the first assertion, `Stacks.Blowup.isPullback_blowUpChart`, this completes tag
0804. -/
@[stacks 0804 "b⁻¹(U) is covered by the spectra of the affine blowup algebras"]
theorem iSup_opensRange_blowUpAffineChart (U : S.affineOpens) :
    ⨆ r : ℐ.ideal U, (blowUpAffineChart ℐ U r.2).opensRange
      = blowUpToBase ℐ ⁻¹ᵁ (U : S.Opens) := by
  rw [blowUpToBase_preimage_coe]
  simp only [blowUpAffineChart, Scheme.Hom.opensRange_comp, ← Scheme.Hom.image_iSup,
    iSup_opensRange_specAffineBlowupι, Scheme.Hom.image_top_eq_opensRange]

end Stacks.Blowup

